Z||000000||fiero56||05-21-2001||06:12 PM|||| <A HREF="http://moneycentral.msn.com/articles/news/mondays/6938.asp?package=moneymonday" TARGET=_blank>http://moneycentral.msn.com/articles/news/mondays/6938.asp?package=moneymonday</A> <P>What a load of crap! The dudes Mazda prolly had a 10 gal tank. His new mini-van probably gets the same mileage as his Mazda did, maybe better. But because his mini-van has a larger tank, he's bitching about paying more to fill it up at the pump. Its amazing the people who are able to get a college degree and get paid to write such garbage. And to all those electric car people, energy is neither created nor destroyed. Most places, rather than burn gasoline in their car, they burn coal to charge their electric vehicle. I don't know what electric prices are, but I bet that costs a fortune too. And don't get me started on these gas/electric hybrids. I think hydrogen is the only option even worth looking into.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sootah||05-21-2001||06:54 PM||||Solar power would also be worth looking into, allthough I don't think it will be a viable option for many years to come. My main consern with hydrogen is the high explosive factor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||05-21-2001||08:50 PM||||I agree. Those electric car people havent figured out it costs to recharge them. I heard something about a surcharge in california now of a couple of dollars a day added to electric bill. And its not all that cheap to haul around a 2000 pnds of batteries. Lets see, some rough guesswork=25 12 volt batteries to buy every 3 or 4 years at say $75 @ for deep cycle is only $1875.00. ill keep my gasser thank you.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||05-21-2001||10:28 PM||||They had on the local news tonight about a guy who bought an electric golf cart, and turned it into a street legal golf-cart. He has the correct lighting, seat belts, lisc plates, etc. It has a 15mph top speed(street legal?!?!?), and he uses it as his daily driver around the city. He figures he is saving over $500 in gas per month. All I can say is, either he gets about 1mpg on his previous vehicle, or he drives a $hit-load of miles, which if thats the case, why is his new vehicle only capable of 15mph. Some people come up with crazy solutions to problems.||||reg||1
